---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="Taxonomy and Scope | Aerial Atlas" description="How Aerial Atlas classifies cable transport systems.">
	<section class="panel page-head">
		<p class="pill">Methodology</p>
		<h1>Clear taxonomy beats vague cable car labels.</h1>
		<p>
			People search with broad language, but strong discovery needs technical precision. Aerial Atlas stores strict
			types while still supporting ambiguous terms in search.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="grid">
		<article class="panel item">
			<h2>Aerial tramway</h2>
			<p>Cabins shuttle back and forth on fixed support cables with a separate haul rope.</p>
			<p class="meta">Best for scenic spans, dramatic climbs, and iconic two-cabin experiences.</p>
		</article>
		<article class="panel item">
			<h2>Gondola lift</h2>
			<p>Small cabins circulate continuously on a moving cable, usually with higher frequency.</p>
			<p class="meta">Best for network-style movement and urban backbone coverage.</p>
		</article>
		<article class="panel item">
			<h2>Funicular</h2>
			<p>Rail-based cars on a steep slope are cable-connected and counterbalanced.</p>
			<p class="meta">Best treated as a related but separate branch of cable transport.</p>
		</article>
	</section>

	<section class="panel principles">
		<h2>Build principles</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Separate scenic rides from commuter systems so recommendations match intent.</li>
			<li>Prioritize operational fields like weather sensitivity and departure model.</li>
			<li>Treat accessibility as structured data, not a single yes or no flag.</li>
			<li>Pair practical planning with history, engineering, and fun facts.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
	.page-head {
		padding: 1.3rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.7rem;
	}
	.page-head p {
		max-width: 70ch;
	}
	.grid {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 0.85rem;
	}
	.item {
		padding: 1rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.6rem;
	}
	.item h2 {
		font-size: 1.3rem;
	}
	.meta {
		font-size: 0.92rem;
		color: var(--steel);
	}
	.principles {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		padding: 1.2rem;
	}
	.principles ul {
		margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
		padding-left: 1rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.5rem;
	}
	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		.grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
